.\docs\actionsunning-actions.md:30:While an action runs for a card, that card's entry points are disabled — one action at a time per card. This state is in memory only, so nothing is left disabled after a restart.
.\docs\actions\placeholders.md:47:- A card placeholder only resolves when the action runs with card context. Use `appliesTo` with `"kind": "card"` so an action that needs `{{card-file}}` or `{{this-card}}` is only offered where it makes sense.
.\designeleases\0_3_0\B_107_websocket_agent_selection.md:43:- Agent controls remain disabled while host config or availability is loading. They become enabled after both loads succeed and no action run prevents editing.
.\designeleases\0_0_4\J_025_move_action_popup_state_to_leaf_owners.md:54:- Prove another card/action run cannot render this popup.
.\designeleases\0_0_4\J_024_replace_execution_state_with_scoped_action_runs.md:5:title: replace global execution state with scoped action runs
.\designeleases\0_0_4\J_024_replace_execution_state_with_scoped_action_runs.md:56:- Preserve per-card persistence: `card__<cardId>.json` contains all action runs and conversations for that card.
.\designeleases\0_0_3\F_64_agent_actions.md:15:Execute `agent` actions through the Electron action runner with run-specific prompt input, one structured process per turn, cancellation, history for the same action id/context, and conversion of custom prompts to reusable definitions.
.\designeleases\0_0_3\F_64_agent_actions.md:23:- The popup sends the action `id`, context, and run-specific agent/model/thinking-level and extra-prompt input to the Electron action runner. It does not send the persisted `prompt` or executable agent command.
.\designeleases\0_0_3\F_64_agent_actions.md:29:- Cancelling the action asks the Electron action runner to stop the agent process and chain.
.\designeleases\0_0_3\F_63_electron_action_execution_and_chaining.md:15:Move the complete action runner to Electron. Electron resolves a persisted action by stable id, prepares its worktree when requested, executes command or agent actions, orchestrates `onBefore`/main/`on`/`onAfter`, streams phase-specific events, and supports cancellation.
.\designeleases\0_0_3\F_63_electron_action_execution_and_chaining.md:23:- Add one Electron `ActionRunner` used by manual, `onState`, scheduled, and related-action runs.
.\designeleases\0_0_3\F_63_electron_action_execution_and_chaining.md:28:- Delegate agent-process lifecycle to the Electron agent runner while retaining chain ownership in the Electron action runner.
.\designeleases\0_0_3\F_63_electron_action_execution_and_chaining.md:40:- Manual, state-triggered, scheduled, and related-action runs share one Electron action runner.
.\designeleases\0_0_3\F_65_state_triggers_and_folder_watching.md:23:- When a card changes to an `onState` value, request the matching action `id` through the Electron action runner with the card context.
